{"tool_name":"2d-gaussian-fitting-macro-(fijiimagej)-for-multiple-signals.","contents":["neubias"],"fetched_metadata":{"neubias":{"body":[{"format":"basic_html","processed":"<p>This script includes a rough feature detection and then fine 2D Gaussian algorithm to fit Gaussians within detected regions. This macro is unique because the ImageJ/Fiji curve fitting API only supports 1-D curve. I get around this by&nbsp;linearising the equation. This&nbsp;implementation is for isotropic (spherical) or anistropic (longer in x/y) diagonally covariant Gaussians but not fully covariant Gaussians (anisotropic and rotated).&nbsp;</p>","summary":"","value":"<p>This script includes a rough feature detection and then fine 2D Gaussian algorithm to fit Gaussians within detected regions. This macro is unique because the ImageJ/Fiji curve fitting API only supports 1-D curve. I get around this by&nbsp;linearising the equation. This&nbsp;implementation is for isotropic (spherical) or anistropic (longer in x/y) diagonally covariant Gaussians but not fully covariant Gaussians (anisotropic and rotated).&nbsp;</p>\r\n"}],"changed":[{"format":"Y-m-d\\TH:i:sP","value":"2021-03-16T21:06:27+00:00"}],"created":[{"format":"Y-m-d\\TH:i:sP","value":"2018-10-17T17:13:31+00:00"}],"default_langcode":[{"value":true}],"attribution_instructions":[],"comments_2023":[],"free_tagging":[],"give_feedback_on_this_soft":[{"cid":0,"comment_count":0,"last_comment_name":null,"last_comment_timestamp":1539797010,"last_comment_uid":3118,"status":2}],"has_author":[{"value":"Waithe dominic orcid.org/0000-0003-2685-4226"}],"has_biological_terms":[],"has_comparison":[],"has_documentation":[{"options":[],"title":"Link to ReadMe text.","uri":"https://github.com/dwaithe/generalMacros"},{"options":[],"title":"Related Wikipedia article.","uri":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gaussian_function"}],"has_doi":[],"has_entry_curator":[{"target_id":3118,"target_type":"user","target_uuid":"57948909-261b-4805-8926-1fdc3f47e2d1","url":"/u